WEBVTT

1
00:10:43.661 --> 00:10:47.828
Are you Henry?

2
00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.327
Yes.

3
00:10:50.578 --> 00:10:53.161
Girl named Mary called
on the pay-phone.

4
00:10:53.244 --> 00:10:56.786
Said she said her parents
and you are invited to dinner.

5
00:10:59.494 --> 00:11:00.744
Oh, yeah?

6
00:11:11.161 --> 00:11:12.411
Thank you very much.

7
00:17:18.361 --> 00:17:20.445
You're late, Henry.

8
00:17:27.736 --> 00:17:32.111
I didn't know if you wanted me
to come or not. Where have you been?

9
00:17:39.195 --> 00:17:40.861
You never come
around anymore.

10
00:17:55.444 --> 00:17:56.903
Dinner's almost ready.

11
00:18:13.778 --> 00:18:14.403
Come on in.

12
00:18:41.486 --> 00:18:42.944
Hello there.

13
00:18:44.611 --> 00:18:46.278
Hello.

14
00:18:49.402 --> 00:18:51.278
I'm very pleased to meet you.

15
00:18:55.236 --> 00:18:56.694
Sit down.

16
00:19:25.028 --> 00:19:27.111
It's Henry. isn't it?

17
00:19:29.195 --> 00:19:30.444
Yes.

18
00:19:49.195 --> 00:19:54.195
Mary tells me you're a very
nice fellow. What do you do?

19
00:19:56.278 --> 00:19:58.361
I-I am on vacation.

20
00:20:00.444 --> 00:20:02.111
What did you do?

21
00:20:04.195 --> 00:20:05.444
Oh, I'm sorry.

22
00:20:08.361 --> 00:20:11.694
I work in Lapell's factory.

23
00:20:14.611 --> 00:20:16.278
I'm a printer.

24
00:20:16.694 --> 00:20:20.028
Henry is very clever at printing.

25
00:20:23.361 --> 00:20:25.861
Yes, he sounds very clever.

26
00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:38.778
I thought I heard a stranger.

27
00:20:38.986 --> 00:20:43.236
We've got chicken tonight. Strangest
damn things, they're man-made.

28
00:20:43.277 --> 00:20:45.861
Little damn things,
smaller than my fist.

29
00:20:45.903 --> 00:20:48.361
But they're new.

30
00:20:49.402 --> 00:20:50.444
I'm Bill.

31
00:20:52.736 --> 00:20:57.945
- Hello, I'm Henry.
- Henry is at Lapell's factory.

32
00:20:58.153 --> 00:21:00.444
Printing's your business, huh?
Plumbing is mine.

33
00:21:00.486 --> 00:21:05.236
30 years. I've seen this neighbourhood change
from pastures to the hell-hole it is now!

34
00:21:05.277 --> 00:21:07.945
I put every damn pipe
in this neighborhood.

35
00:21:07.986 --> 00:21:09.195
- Dad!
- Bill!

36
00:21:09.236 --> 00:21:13.361
And people think pipes grow in their home,
well they sure as hell don't! Look at my knees.

37
00:21:14.611 --> 00:21:17.945
- Look at my knees!
- Bill!

38
00:21:19.486 --> 00:21:22.945
- Are you hungry?
- Bill!

39
00:23:38.778 --> 00:23:41.694
The girls had heard this before...

40
00:23:41.903 --> 00:23:46.277
but 14 years ago, I had
an operation on my arm here.

41
00:23:46.486 --> 00:23:51.486
Doctors said I wouldn't be able to use it.
But what the hell do they know, I said.

42
00:23:51.694 --> 00:23:57.945
And I rubbed it for a half hour every day
and then I got so as... I could move it a little.

43
00:23:58.152 --> 00:24:03.986
And I got so as... so I could turn a faucet
and pretty soon I had my arm back again.

44
00:24:04.611 --> 00:24:08.569
Now I can't feel a damn
thing in it. All numb...

45
00:24:13.361 --> 00:24:17.528
I'm afraid to cut it, you know.

46
00:24:17.736 --> 00:24:24.820
Mary usually does the carving but
maybe tonight you'll do it, Henry.

47
00:24:25.861 --> 00:24:28.361
All right with you?

48
00:24:33.152 --> 00:24:34.194
Of course.

49
00:24:37.945 --> 00:24:40.444
I'd be happy to.

50
00:24:47.111 --> 00:24:51.695
I just... just cut them up
like regular chickens?

51
00:24:51.736 --> 00:24:54.194
Sure, just cut them up
like regular chickens.

52
00:25:49.194 --> 00:25:52.528
She'll be all right in a minute.

53
00:25:54.403 --> 00:25:56.278
Excuse me.

54
00:26:31.161 --> 00:26:34.078
Well, Henry, what do you know?

55
00:26:41.369 --> 00:26:43.661
I don't know much of anything.

56
00:27:21.369 --> 00:27:24.494
Henry, may I speak
to you a minute?

57
00:27:24.536 --> 00:27:26.995
Over here.

58
00:28:11.244 --> 00:28:16.578
Did you and Mary
had sexual intercourse?

59
00:28:18.244 --> 00:28:21.995
- Why?
- Did you?

60
00:28:22.619 --> 00:28:26.911
- Why are you asking me this question?
- I have a very good reason.

61
00:28:26.953 --> 00:28:29.911
And now I want you to tell me.

62
00:28:32.411 --> 00:28:36.786
I-I'm very... I love Mary.

63
00:28:36.828 --> 00:28:42.369
Henry, I asked you if you
and Mary had sexual intercourse.

64
00:28:42.411 --> 00:28:46.578
- I-I don't think it's any of your business.
- Henry!

65
00:28:48.244 --> 00:28:50.745
Sorry.

66
00:28:51.995 --> 00:28:56.578
You're in very bad trouble
if you won't cooperate.

67
00:29:03.244 --> 00:29:05.327
Well... I...

68
00:29:07.828 --> 00:29:11.995
- Mary!
- Mother!

69
00:29:13.369 --> 00:29:17.411
- Answer me!
- I'm too nervous.

70
00:29:17.453 --> 00:29:21.578
- There's a baby. It's at the hospital.
- Mom!

71
00:29:21.619 --> 00:29:25.745
- And you're the father.
- It isn't possible...

72
00:29:25.786 --> 00:29:30.536
- They're still not sure it is a baby.
- It's premature, but there's a baby.

73
00:29:30.578 --> 00:29:35.745
After the two of you are married which should
be very soon, you can pick the baby up.

74
00:29:50.327 --> 00:29:52.828
Mom, he's got a nose bleed.

75
00:29:57.828 --> 00:29:59.911
I'll get ice.

76
00:30:04.911 --> 00:30:10.536
You don't mind do you Henry,
I mean about getting married?

77
00:30:11.786 --> 00:30:13.244
No!

78
00:30:24.911 --> 00:30:27.828
This dinner's getting mighty cold.

79
00:36:19.702 --> 00:36:21.578
Is there any mail?

80
00:36:25.786 --> 00:36:26.994
No.

81
00:39:38.245 --> 00:39:40.120
Shut up!

82
00:39:44.494 --> 00:39:46.994
Shut up!

83
00:40:55.120 --> 00:40:58.661
I can't stand it.
I'm going home.

84
00:41:02.203 --> 00:41:07.828
- What are you talking about?
- I can't even sleep. I'm losing my mind.

85
00:41:08.286 --> 00:41:13.036
You're on vacation, now.
You can take care of it for a night.

86
00:41:13.078 --> 00:41:16.161
Will you come back tomorrow?

87
00:41:16.203 --> 00:41:19.911
All I need is a decent night's sleep.

88
00:41:29.286 --> 00:41:33.869
Why don't you just stay home?

89
00:41:33.911 --> 00:41:37.203
I'll do what I wanna do.

90
00:41:37.245 --> 00:41:42.203
And you better take real good
care of things while I'm gone.

91
00:45:07.736 --> 00:45:09.611
Oh, you are sick...

92
00:53:10.244 --> 00:53:12.619
Move over.

93
00:53:48.036 --> 00:53:52.619
Move over.
Move over!

94
00:58:01.995 --> 00:58:04.911
I locked myself
out of my apartment.

95
00:58:21.369 --> 00:58:24.286
And it's so late.

96
00:59:24.286 --> 00:59:26.369
Where's your wife?

97
00:59:37.411 --> 00:59:41.369
She must've gone
back to her parents, again.

98
00:59:45.120 --> 00:59:47.619
I'm not sure.

99
01:00:42.411 --> 01:00:45.327
Can I spend the night here?

100
01:03:07.202 --> 01:03:13.453
In heaven everything is fine

101
01:03:14.077 --> 01:03:20.327
In heaven everything is fine

102
01:03:20.536 --> 01:03:22.619
In heaven everything is fine

103
01:03:27.411 --> 01:03:36.161
You've got your good things
and I've got mine

104
01:03:40.536 --> 01:03:46.578
In heaven everything is fine

105
01:03:47.202 --> 01:03:53.244
In heaven everything is fine

106
01:03:53.453 --> 01:04:00.328
In heaven everything is fine

107
01:04:00.953 --> 01:04:06.786
You've got your good things
and you've got mine

108
01:04:13.661 --> 01:04:26.161
In heaven...
...everything is fine

109
01:09:28.244 --> 01:09:31.161
Ok, Paul!

110
01:09:38.453 --> 01:09:41.578
Hiya sonny,
what you got there?

111
01:10:05.119 --> 01:10:07.619
Counter, Paul!

112
01:12:24.619 --> 01:12:27.120
It's OK.
